:ARCHIVE_OLPATH: Modify Uart so that do not need interrupt/polling
:ARCHIVE_CATEGORY: lab_driver
:END:
With interrupt we have: uartintr (read one byte) -> consoleintr (triger console read when \n is hit) -> consoleread

But now we do not have interrupt, the logs chanegs to
consoleread continuously reading char directly from uart and yield while spin on uart.
 xv6 already has uartgetc() that returns -1 if no byte is available.
#+begin_src c
acquire(&cons.lock);
while (n > 0) {
  for (;;) {
    // Drop the lock before polling + feeding consoleintr()
    release(&cons.lock);

    int c;
    while ((c = uartgetc()) != -1) {
      consoleintr(c);         // consoleintr() takes cons.lock itself
    }

    acquire(&cons.lock);
    if (cons.r != cons.w)     // data arrived
      break;

    if (killed(myproc())) {
      release(&cons.lock);
      return -1;
    }

    // Cooperative: don’t spin forever
    release(&cons.lock);
    yield();
    acquire(&cons.lock);
  }

  // …consume from cons.buf as usual…
}
release(&cons.lock);

#+end_src


#+begin_src

#+end_src
